Fix a verifier crash ("undeclared identifier: $heap") when the condition of a let-such-that expression reads no heap but contains a lambda that calls a function (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/362). The axiom of the let's `$canCall` function now translates such a condition with the placeholder heap of heap-independent definitions, as the bodies of those definitions are translated, instead of a heap variable it does not bind.
